From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:02:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: notify ubus when a removed affiliated AP leaves the
 links of its stations

hostapd_free_link_stas() frees the link stations of an affiliated AP
that leaves the AP MLD: at the expiry of its removal (603), from the
OpenWrt ucode.c before the link stops, and from hostapd_free_stas()
when the BSS goes down. The non-AP MLDs stay associated over their
other links, and ap_free_link_sta() drops the link from their other
stations (199), but nothing tells a ubus subscriber, which keeps the
links of the last sta-authorized or sta-links-changed.

Send sta-links-changed for the station of the association link once
the link station is freed.

This depends on 604 (hostapd_ubus_notify_sta_links()) and on 199
(ap_free_link_sta() in hostapd_free_link_stas()).

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -691,7 +691,8 @@ void ap_free_link_sta(struct hostapd_dat
 
 void hostapd_free_link_stas(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 {
-	struct sta_info *sta, *prev;
+	struct hostapd_data *assoc_hapd;
+	struct sta_info *sta, *prev, *assoc_sta;
 
 	sta = hapd->sta_list;
 	while (sta) {
@@ -705,7 +706,10 @@ void hostapd_free_link_stas(struct hosta
 			   MAC2STR(prev->addr));
 		ap_sta_link_event(hapd, WPA_EVENT_LINK_STA_REMOVED, prev->addr,
 				  hapd->mld_link_id);
+		assoc_sta = hostapd_ml_get_assoc_sta(hapd, prev, &assoc_hapd);
 		ap_free_link_sta(hapd, prev);
+		if (assoc_sta && assoc_sta != prev)
+			hostapd_ubus_notify_sta_links(assoc_hapd, assoc_sta);
 	}
 }
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
